From 2e5de68b6a96019cca9c2ed175b9412a12ed6b05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:47:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(worker): preallocate contiguous CUDA pool on 64 KiB UMA

On ARM64 64 KiB unified-memory hosts with iommu.passthrough=0, hundreds
of separate cudaMalloc or 2 MiB cuMemCreate allocations interleave
immortal ARM SMMU L3 page-table pages (SecPageTables) inside freshly
converted MIGRATE_UNMOVABLE 512 MiB buddy pageblocks, permanently
shattering order-13 contiguity after a single boot.

Pre-reserve one 512 MiB-aligned contiguous CUDA caching-allocator
segment in Worker.init_device when native cudaMalloc caching is active
on a 64 KiB host with >= 32 GiB of order-13 blocks free, pin it with a
2 MiB large-pool anchor so empty_cache() does not release it before
weights bind, bypass _scoped_allocator_max_split(20) during load_model,
and skip redundant buddy soaking in direct_loader.bind_weight_arena
while placing the dense weight arena at the aligned front of the pool.

Upstream-base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Quality: no numerical or algorithmic change; memory placement only.
Tests: pytest tests/v1/worker/test_contiguous_cuda_pool.py
       tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_direct_loader.py
       tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_direct_loader_cuda.py
       tests/v1/worker/test_engine_grid_sync.py (100 passed).
Upstream-status: local candidate-63 patch.
